# Vercel Speed Insights Implementation

## Summary
Successfully installed and configured Vercel Speed Insights for this Next.js project by following the latest official documentation from Vercel.

## Changes Made

### 1. Package Installation
- **File:** `package.json` and `package-lock.json`
- **Action:** Installed `@vercel/speed-insights` package via npm
- **Version:** Latest compatible version added to dependencies

### 2. SpeedInsights Component Integration
- **File:** `app/layout.tsx`
- **Actions:**
  - Added import statement: `import { SpeedInsights } from "@vercel/speed-insights/next";`
  - Added `<SpeedInsights />` component in the body section, positioned after the existing `<Analytics />` component
  
### 3. Implementation Details
- **Framework:** Next.js v16.2.7 with App Router
- **Integration Method:** Added SpeedInsights component to the root layout file following the official Next.js integration pattern
- **Placement:** Component placed inside the `<body>` tag alongside the existing Vercel Analytics component
- **Import Source:** Used `@vercel/speed-insights/next` for Next.js-specific optimizations

## Verification Steps Completed

✅ Build test: Successfully built the project with `npm run build`
✅ Linting: Passed ESLint checks with no errors
✅ Type checking: TypeScript compilation successful
✅ Lock files: Updated package-lock.json for dependency consistency

## Next Steps for Activation

To enable Speed Insights data collection:
1. Enable Speed Insights in your Vercel project dashboard
2. Deploy the application to Vercel
3. Speed Insights will automatically start collecting performance metrics after user visits

## Notes

- The implementation follows the official Vercel documentation from https://vercel.com/docs/speed-insights/quickstart
- SpeedInsights component is positioned after Analytics component to maintain logical ordering
- No breaking changes introduced - existing functionality preserved
- The component integrates seamlessly with the existing Vercel Analytics setup
